  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Fifteen strikeouts and five hits. The game stayed tied until the tenth, when the Padres' bats finally woke up and the Yankees' bullpen cracked.",
    "what_this_means": "The offense was starved for air all night. Max Fried gave them exactly what they deserved. One earned run in 5.2 innings, precision without mercy. Will Warren bridged the next 2.1 innings clean. Then Paul Blackburn walked in from the pen with the game still knotted at one, and gave up the go-ahead run on a single swing. Spencer Jones had answered with a go-ahead single in the tenth, a chance the Yankees manufactured but couldn't convert. Ben Rice went 3-for-4 with a homer, kept them alive, made the game look closer than it felt. But three hits in ten innings is not an offense. It's a locked door. The bullpen held until it didn't. Now they're four back, and the pattern is getting louder.",
    "what_to_watch": "Robbie Ray takes the mound tonight for San Diego, a 3.14 ERA guy who doesn't miss. Carlos Rod\u00f3n has been sharp. 2.09 over his last four starts. But the Yankees' bats have to show they're awake before the starter even matters.",
